      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like jetski doesn\u0027t like the idea of do runtime check. I kind agree with it, here is the summary I got from jetski\n\n```\nNo, we should not check that the reserved slots are zero-initialized at runtime:\n\n - Compiler guarantee: Drivers declare static const struct apf_ops with designated initializers. Under ISO C99 §6.7.8, any struct member omitted from the initializer list is guaranteed by the compiler to be initialized to zero in .rodata.\n\n- Future breakage: When a slot is eventually consumed in a future release via ANDROID_KABI_USE(1, ...), newer drivers implementing that callback will set it to a non-zero function pointer. A runtime check asserting that reserved slots must be zero would reject those drivers.\n\n - Standard GKI pattern: None of the other KABI-padded structures in GKI (net_device_ops, ethtool_ops, pkvm_module_ops, etc.) inspect reserved padding at runtime. When a slot is consumed, the kernel simply checks `if (ops-\u003enew_callback)`.\n\n```",
